From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:19:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: validate radar, thermal and WED RRO event lengths

mt7996_mcu_rx_event() only guarantees the receive descriptor fields used
for dispatch. mt7996_mcu_rx_radar_detected(), mt7996_mcu_rx_thermal_notify()
and mt7996_mcu_wed_rro_event() then read event fields after the descriptor
without checking the event length. A truncated event causes an out-of-bounds
read.

Ignore events too short for the fields the handler reads, like the other
unsolicited event handlers do.

Port of upstream commit cd0c5fdf01b33b89a4a8435a98de88b0823b16a4 ("wifi: mt76:
mt7996: validate radar, thermal and WED RRO event lengths"), which is newer
than the pinned mt76 2026-10-08~639e1287 tree.  The guards are unchanged; the
hunks are re-anchored to this tree and carry a little more trailing context so
the series still applies with `patch -F0`.

Fixes: 98686cd21624 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: add driver for MediaTek Wi-Fi 7 (802.11be) devices")
Fixes: 21f290884bc1 ("wifi: mt76: connac: add thermal protection support for mt7996")
Fixes: a5d028d66836 ("wifi: mt76: mt7996: add wed rro delete session garbage collector")
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20261024071927.2279668-5-nbd@nbd.name
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -781,6 +781,9 @@
 	struct mt76_phy *mphy = &dev->mt76.phy;
 	struct mt7996_mcu_rdd_report *r;
 
+	if (skb->len < offsetofend(struct mt7996_mcu_rdd_report, rdd_idx))
+		return;
+
 	r = (struct mt7996_mcu_rdd_report *)skb->data;
 
 	switch (r->rdd_idx) {
@@ -1039,6 +1042,10 @@
 	struct mt7996_mcu_thermal_notify *n;
 	struct mt7996_phy *phy;
 
+	if (skb->len < offsetofend(struct mt7996_mcu_thermal_notify,
+				   duty_percent))
+		return;
+
 	n = (struct mt7996_mcu_thermal_notify *)skb->data;
 
 	if (le16_to_cpu(n->tag) != THERMAL_NOTIFY_TAG)
@@ -1095,7 +1102,7 @@
 {
 	struct mt7996_mcu_wed_rro_event *event = (void *)skb->data;
 
-	if (!mt7996_has_hwrro(dev))
+	if (!mt7996_has_hwrro(dev) || skb->len < sizeof(*event))
 		return;
 
 	skb_pull(skb, sizeof(struct mt7996_mcu_rxd) + 4);
